  "question": {
    "text": "Calgon is used for water treatment. Which of the following statement is NOT true about Calgon?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NImbn",
      "text": "It is polymeric compound and is water soluble.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "U5fl3",
      "text": "Calgon contains the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math> most abundant element by weight in the Earth&#39;s crust.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OHGuT",
      "text": "It is also known as Graham&#39;s salt.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dkYs1",
      "text": "It doesnot remove <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion by precipitation.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math> most abundant element is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Si</mi></math> and it is not present in calgon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>18</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;(Graham&#39;s salt)(Sodium hexametaphosphate)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> It exist in polymeric form as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NaPO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></math> and water soluble compound</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> It removes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in soluble ion but not by precipitation</p>",
    "image": null
